From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:50:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] dri/android: offer a config whose only buffer is eight bits
 of stencil

Android's hardware renderer asks for a stencil buffer of eight bits and no
depth buffer for every window it draws, and the DRI screen offered no config
that fits: every config with stencil also had a depth plane, so the window's
depth-stencil buffer held a 32-bit float depth beside the stencil, four to
eight bytes per pixel where one is wanted.

Add PIPE_FORMAT_S8_UINT to the depth-stencil formats an Android screen offers
when the driver can render to it. The configs it makes have no depth bits and
eight stencil bits, which eglChooseConfig sorts before the configs that have a
depth plane for a request that wants none. A host that does not offer the
format, as an older virglrenderer does not, leaves the config list as it was.

The state tracker did not treat the stencil plane of such a window as the
drawable's depth-stencil attachment. A window framebuffer keeps a renderbuffer
whose format has no depth at BUFFER_STENCIL alone, and only BUFFER_DEPTH maps to
the drawable's depth-stencil attachment, so no framebuffer asked the drawable
for the plane and each one allocated a stencil buffer of its own. Contexts that
draw to one window then did not see each other's stencil values, which the
multi-context EGL render cases do not accept. Map a stencil-only window
renderbuffer to the drawable's depth-stencil attachment when the framebuffer
is built and when it is validated, as a depth-stencil one is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 src/mesa/state_tracker/st_manager.c    | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c
index 7855f4b2b27d6795de4cbe7795d54ed669dcfba7..c973f511e3714787d84ddd3d820406ef6bab4202 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/dri/dri_screen.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include "dri_context.h"
 #include "dri_helpers.h"
 
+#include "util/detect_os.h"
 #include "util/u_inlines.h"
 #include "pipe/p_screen.h"
 #include "util/format/u_formats.h"
@@ -342,7 +343,7 @@ dri_fill_in_modes(struct dri_screen *screen)
       PIPE_FORMAT_R4G4B4A4_UNORM,
    };
    struct dri_config **configs = NULL;
-   enum pipe_format zs_formats[5];
+   enum pipe_format zs_formats[6];
    unsigned num_zs_formats = 0;
    unsigned i;
    struct pipe_screen *p_screen = screen->base.screen;
@@ -385,6 +386,17 @@ dri_fill_in_modes(struct dri_screen *screen)
    else if (HAS_ZS(Z32_FLOAT))
       zs_formats[num_zs_formats++] = PIPE_FORMAT_Z32_FLOAT;
 
+#if DETECT_OS_ANDROID
+   /* Android's hardware renderer asks for a stencil buffer of eight bits and
+    * no depth for every window, and a config with only that stores one byte
+    * per pixel where the smallest one with a depth plane stores four. An
+    * eglChooseConfig that wants no depth sorts it before every config that has
+    * one.
+    */
+   if (HAS_ZS(S8_UINT))
+      zs_formats[num_zs_formats++] = PIPE_FORMAT_S8_UINT;
+#endif
+
 #undef HAS_ZS
 
    mixed_color_depth =
diff --git a/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_manager.c b/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_manager.c
index 9af523a90a962a6e026a188e924646c34bfcdc6b..c3f6c64deb6ca104ee477703b99ef407ef28a003 100644
--- a/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_manager.c
+++ b/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_manager.c
@@ -261,6 +261,12 @@ st_framebuffer_validate(struct gl_framebuffer *stfb,
          continue;
       }
 
+      /* The depth-stencil attachment of a stencil-only visual is at
+       * BUFFER_STENCIL.
+       */
+      if (idx == BUFFER_DEPTH && !stfb->Attachment[idx].Renderbuffer)
+         idx = BUFFER_STENCIL;
+
       rb = stfb->Attachment[idx].Renderbuffer;
       assert(rb);
       if (rb->texture == textures[i] &&
@@ -324,6 +330,17 @@ st_framebuffer_update_attachments(struct gl_framebuffer *stfb)
          continue;
 
       statt = buffer_index_to_attachment(idx);
+
+      /* A visual whose depth-stencil format has no depth keeps its
+       * renderbuffer at BUFFER_STENCIL alone. It is still the drawable's
+       * depth-stencil attachment: left out, every framebuffer the contexts of
+       * one drawable make would allocate a stencil plane of its own instead of
+       * sharing the drawable's.
+       */
+      if (idx == BUFFER_STENCIL &&
+          !stfb->Attachment[BUFFER_DEPTH].Renderbuffer)
+         statt = ST_ATTACHMENT_DEPTH_STENCIL;
+
       if (statt != ST_ATTACHMENT_INVALID &&
           st_visual_have_buffers(stfb->drawable->visual, 1 << statt))
          stfb->statts[stfb->num_statts++] = statt;
